    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6c0cfb6c-0898-5687-b72f-8e4de58cf454",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -6 & 40 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 20\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -6 & 40 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 20\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{40}{3} \\\\ 2 & -3 & 20\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{40}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{20}{3}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=\\frac{40}{3} \\\\ y &=-\\frac{20}{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-\\frac{20}{3}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2\\left(-\\frac{20}{3}\\right)=\\frac{40}{3}\\,\\Rightarrow\\,x=\\frac{40}{3}-\\frac{40}{3}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=0$ and $y=-\\frac{20}{3}.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
